# DAG: matched-family (IMRPhenomXAS) injection NS validation on the
# ls_min_q=0.06-fixed checkpoints, for both representations.
#
# RETRAIN builds checkpoints/phenomd_nonspinning_dense30_exact_xas_lsminq006.pt
# (the exact/plus-cross+XAS analogue of the already-existing
# phase_amplitude_xas_lsminq006 checkpoint). EXACT_WITHK/EXACT_NOK need
# that checkpoint, so they're children of RETRAIN. PA_WITHK/PA_NOK use the
# already-trained phase-amplitude checkpoint and have no dependency, so
# they run immediately in parallel with RETRAIN.
#
# Submit from /scratch/wiay/daniel/heron-dense45 on wiay:
#   condor_submit_dag condor/dag_matched_lsminq006.dag
# Monitor: condor_q daniel -all ; tail -f condor/dag_matched_lsminq006.dag.dagman.out

JOB RETRAIN    condor/train_exact_xas_lsminq006.sub
JOB PA_WITHK   condor/pa_xas_lsminq006_matched_withK.sub
JOB PA_NOK     condor/pa_xas_lsminq006_matched_noK.sub
JOB EXACT_WITHK condor/exact_xas_lsminq006_matched_withK.sub
JOB EXACT_NOK   condor/exact_xas_lsminq006_matched_noK.sub

PARENT RETRAIN CHILD EXACT_WITHK EXACT_NOK

RETRY RETRAIN 1
RETRY EXACT_WITHK 1
RETRY EXACT_NOK 1
RETRY PA_WITHK 1
RETRY PA_NOK 1
